{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patch set 1 took Verified -1. Two real CI failures, both fixed in patch set 2 - neither was caught by the plan's enumerated regression list, so recording them:\n\n1) Prompt-index drift gate. src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json is a DERIVED file, regenerated from the prompt front-matter ('No hand-edited catalog - the index is derived'). The ticket's move 5 said to correct the ticket-quality description string at index.json line 82, but editing the derived file alone leaves it out of sync with its source. Fixed by editing the front-matter in src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_quality.md and running 'python -m rebar.llm.prompting.prompts regenerate-index'. The regenerated index is byte-identical to the hand-edit, so only the source file changed - source and derived now agree and the gate passes.\n\n2) Optionality lean-lane: 'degradation-path tests run with NO agents extra'. tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_optionality.py:173 drove the review_ticket CLI arm as main(['review', epic, 'ticket-quality']) - a positional reviewer, which the shim now rejects with SystemExit(2). The ticket's scope named line 207 of this file but not line 173.\n\nFixing the argv was not sufficient, and the reason is a genuine contract change worth recording: without the agents extra 'rebar review <id>' no longer emits a bare 'Error: ... agents' line on stderr. It forwards to review-plan, whose DETERMINISTIC floor runs BEFORE the LLM tier is needed, so the command emits a plan_review_verdict and the missing extra is reported inside it as coverage.llm_unavailable=true + coverage.llm_error, while stderr carries only the deprecation line and an llm-degrade note. Exit is still non-zero (1), so the invariant that suite exists to protect - automation must not read a missing-extra run as a successful review - still holds.\n\nFixed by adding a _CLI_SHIMMED carve-out mirroring the existing _FAIL_SAFE pattern, asserting the shim's real contract: non-zero exit, no traceback, 'agents' named in the output, and '\"llm_unavailable\": true' present in the verdict. That is a MORE specific assertion than the 'Error:' substring it replaces, not a weaker one. The LIBRARY op's degradation contract is untouched and still pinned by test_library_operation_degrades_without_extra.\n\nReproduced both failures locally before fixing: built a clean venv with 'pip install .' plus only pytest/jsonschema/mcp (agents_extra_installed() == False) and ran the exact CI lane. Now 19 passed there, and 29 passed / 11 skipped in the full-extra lane.\n\nAlso re-ran every CI-only derived-file gate locally: prompt-index, env-registry, mcp-reference, docs-index, readme-quickstart, comment-hygiene - all OK.\n\nPatch set 2 pushed to change 1407."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785901048120460001,"uuid":"6f5da5ed-fdfa-4fb6-92b7-036277b6dade"}